foundation.question_text:
The graph below shows the simple interest earned over time on a $\$2000$ investment.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[below right,font=\small] {$t\text{ (years)}$};
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above left,font=\small] {$I\text{ (\$)}$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} \node[below,font=\small] at (\x,0) {$\x$};
\foreach \y/\v in {1/100,2/200,3/300,4/400,5/500} \node[left,font=\small] at (0,\y) {$\v$};
\node[below left,font=\small] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0) -- (5,5);
\fill[blue] (4,4) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use the graph to find the interest earned after $4$ years.

